    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for LawDog hinges on leveraging favorable matchups against middling starters, with **Matt Chapman** leading the charge at a 68.34 efficiency score. His placement in the lead-off spot against Rodriguez, Ed, combined with a significant BvP historical edge (29 PA) and a friendly park factor, makes him our anchor. Similarly, **Dylan Beavers** (66.63) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.85) provide strong utility and middle infield value. **Perdomo** is particularly well-positioned; his promotion to the two-hole against Mahle provides a calculated +8% order bonus that pushes his profile well into our \"Strong\" start tier, essential for maintaining our aggressive pace in the scarcity-driven SB category.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Cal Raleigh**, who landed just outside the 60+ threshold at 57.16. While his power upside is undeniable, the dynamic platoon penalty against Johnson (R) dragged his efficiency score down enough to make him a marginal play compared to the high-floor versatility of **Taylor Ward** (62.61), who benefits from a +16% park adjustment against Burke, S. We are currently navigating a depleted bench; with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** sequestered on the IL, and **Yainer Diaz** and **Tyler Freeman** absent from today's starting lineups, our depth is thin. We are effectively capped at these starters, meaning we must avoid any late-scratch risks. Monitor the weather at the Burke, S start closely, as any delay could jeopardize our target game counts for the week, but for now, the data confirms a lineup optimized for high-volume, high-efficiency production.",
